      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T05:59:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Update the doc. This is useful if state machine have multiple hierarchy. A -\u003e B -\u003e C. If A is transitioning to C but something wrong happen in B, B can tell its error to C. There is different between StateMachine and SyncStateMachine that SyncStateMachine doesn\u0027t allow changing the target state in the mid way of state transitions but StateMachine can. Thus, StateMachine can just change the target state to error state if error happen in the mid-way.\n\nFor StateMachine, state B can call transitionTo(E) in its enter(). If A calling transitionTo(C), the result would be A -\u003e B -\u003e C -\u003e B -\u003e A -\u003e D -\u003e E.\n  A -\u003e B -\u003e C\n  D -\u003e E\nBut SyncStateMachine will just be A -\u003e B -\u003e C because B won\u0027t allow to call transitionTo in its enter(). Instead B can pass the errorCode to C, then C could decide whether to call transitionTo(E).\n\nAllow changing the target in the mid-way make state transition be very complicated, especially when multiple states all try to change target in the mid-way",
      "parentUuid": "fbbb33af_31412dfd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 53,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 45
      },
